From c57041a44b98b2b35570911ab037ab94ec4741ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build-router <build-router@warslop-dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:56:53 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: per-attempt thinking and menu item provenance

0008 writes one thinking shape into the shared request body before the combo runs, so every fallback attempt carries the head model's value; a plugin that wants each attempt on its own model's native value (jev-router's menu, UP-10c) could only send none or drop backups. onRoute may now return thinking_by_model {<target id>: {control, value}} (same allowlist as 0008, only targets in the final list) and item (a menu id, ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,16}$). With a map, the shared-body write is skipped and the plugin combo's handleSingleModel applies applyPluginRouteThinking(b, pluginAttemptThinking(combo, m)) on each attempt's own body copy; a target the map leaves out gets {control:"none"} (client effort cleared), and the global fallback model is sent with none as well. Without a map, 0008's behaviour is unchanged. buildPluginRouteHeaders adds x-router-item and x-router-thinking (the answering attempt's value, "default" when no field was sent); the 0009 in-band x_omniroute object carries item and thinking too. Unit tests in plugins-onroute and earlyStreamKeepalive.
